ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011KS8.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"53f030670f3ddaef\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNOTE: <strong>The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from 0 to 500</strong>. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"53f030670f3ddaef\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"fb749d8b23b6006c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Report Card: 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"fb749d8b23b6006c\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6f1f0395d6612377\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nLooking at state/jurisdiction performance for eighth-graders in public schools, average scores were lower in 51 states/jurisdictions and not significantly different in 2. This is the largest number of states/jurisdictions with score declines in grade 8 mathematics going back to 2003. Among the states/jurisdictions with score declines, 18 scored lower than the national average score for public school students in 2022; 16 had average scores that were not significantly different from the national public average; and 17 scored higher. Explore detailed state average score results in the NAEP Mathematics Report Card\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6f1f0395d6612377\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b2024dcef58075d8\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT NATION  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b2024dcef58075d8\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011NP8.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a7105b56aceda62c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNOTE: <strong>The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from 0 to 500</strong>. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a7105b56aceda62c\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9b534d3160100a08\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 National Assessment of Educational Progress Grade 8 Mathematics Results\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9b534d3160100a08\">>>", "url": "https://www.fldoe.org/core/fileparse.php/7667/urlt/2022NAEPGrade8Math.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"808b684e9adb9cb0\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNOTE: The NAEP Mathematics scale ranges from <strong>0 to 500</strong>.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"808b684e9adb9cb0\">>>", "siteName": "www.fldoe.org"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775300170589}}
